  "prompt": "For each monthly cohort of accounts created in 2024, what share of the accounts was still paying 6 months later? An account's cohort month is the month of its created_at (Brussels local time); an account created before 2024 belongs to none of these cohorts. An account is paying at a month's end when the sum of its subscription events' mrr_delta_local with event_date on or before that day is above 0. Look at the end of the month 6 calendar months after the cohort month: for the January 2024 cohort, 31 July 2024. The as-of date is 1 January 2026, so every month up to December 2025 has ended. Return four columns, in this order: cohort_month (the first day of the month), cohort_accounts, retained_accounts and retention_rate, retained_accounts divided by cohort_accounts as a fraction between 0 and 1. Return one row for each cohort month of 2024 that has accounts. Any row order is fine.",
